<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk oil port shut due high winds.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk oil port shut due high winds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea closed early on Friday due to bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>Northeasterly winds gusting up to gale force eight shut the 650,000-barrel per day (bpd) port at 0410 (local time) on Friday, the source added.</p>
<p>Two crude vessels were alongside, with three more waiting at anchor outside the port.</p>
<p>Other oil ports at Odessa and Tuapse on the Black Sea, and at Ventspils on the Baltic, were open on Friday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
